WEBVTT

NOTE Customer discovery call — Loopr — Acme Logistics
NOTE Interviewer: Priya Shah (PM). Customer: Dan Reyes, Ops Lead.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:14.480
<v Priya>Thanks for making time, Dan. I want to walk through how your team got started with Loopr last quarter.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:27.330
<v Dan>Yeah, no problem. Honestly the first two weeks were rough. We had four people on the trial and only one of them got past the workspace setup before giving up.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:36.140
<v Priya>What specifically tripped them up? Was it the SSO step or the project import?

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:51.220
<v Dan>The import. The CSV mapper kept rejecting our column headers because we use spaces and your validator wants underscores. Nobody told us that until we hit the error twelve times.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:01:02.910
<v Priya>That's painful. So onboarding friction was real for your team. Did you feel like the docs covered the import format?

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:14.880
<v Dan>The docs exist but they're buried under the "advanced" tab. A new admin isn't going to think CSV import is advanced. That's table-stakes for us.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:23.770
<v Priya>Got it. If we fixed the import path — auto-detect headers, clearer errors — would that change your evaluation?

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:38.560
<v Dan>Honestly yes. The product itself is great once you're in. The routing engine saved us six hours a week on dispatch. It's just the on-ramp that almost killed the pilot.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:46.220
<v Priya>That's good to hear. Can I ask about pricing? You mentioned the procurement team had questions.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:02:01.430
<v Dan>Right. So we have about thirty dispatchers. At fifty dollars a seat per month we can make that work — that's roughly what we pay for the tool we'd be replacing. Anything north of that and we have to escalate to the VP.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:10.180
<v Priya>Fifty per seat is the ceiling that doesn't trigger procurement?

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:21.840
<v Dan>Yeah, $50/seat is fine. Above that we need a business case and that takes a quarter. So if you stay at or under that we can close this in two weeks.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:32.110
<v Priya>Helpful. One more — the onboarding piece, would your dispatchers self-serve a re-do if we shipped a guided import wizard?

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:44.770
<v Dan>If it's actually guided, yes. The current flow assumes you already know what Loopr expects. New users don't. Fix that and you've removed our biggest objection.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.330
<v Priya>Thanks Dan, this is really useful. I'll follow up next week with the wizard mockups.
